## What happens

The test drains the app and checks every Service returned.

At [6351c869](https://github.com/z5labs/humus/commit/6351c86978a51659d1d1dae16a9f4553bd64a712), with go1.27.2 on 4 cores, `flaky stress` ran it 150 times:

|       | load 1 | load 2 |
|-------|--------|--------|
| cpu 1 | 0 / 25 | 0 / 25 |
| cpu 2 | 1 / 25 | 1 / 25 |
| cpu 4 | 0 / 25 | 0 / 25 |

That is 1 failure and 1 hang. Its first failure:

````text
--- FAIL: TestMain_drains (0.31s)
    main_test.go:40: the output had ``` in it
````

It reproduces with:

```sh
flaky stress -tags testcontainers -run '^TestMain_drains$' -shuffle=7 -cpu 2 -load 1 -count 25 ./.
taskset -c 0-1 go -C . test -race -cover -tags testcontainers -count=25 -cpu 2 -timeout 10m0s -run '^TestMain_drains$' -shuffle=7 .
```

It failed only at cpu 2, at either load.

## Why

This hasn't been triaged.

## Expected

`TestMain_drains` passes on every run, at every CPU count and load.

